From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:40:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: sound: apple,s8000-mca: Add the S5L8960X TDM
 speaker link

The iPad mini 2 (J85) plays its speakers through MCA1 of its A7, a TDM
link to two CS35L19 amplifiers, the primary of which provides the bit
and frame clocks from the MCLK the MCA supplies. apple,s5l8960x-mca is
the iPad Air's I2S codec link; add apple,s5l8960x-mca-tdm for this one,
without a bitclock NCO.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
index c2e15fcc5..853055f02 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/apple,s8000-mca.yaml
@@ -26,7 +26,9 @@ description: |
   NCO channel running at twice the bit clock. The S5L8960X (A7) MCA is
   version 1 as well: apple,s5l8960x-mca is the playback-only I2S link of the
   iPad Air to its codec, which provides the bit and frame clocks as on the
-  A9.
+  A9; apple,s5l8960x-mca-tdm the playback-only speaker link (TDM) of the
+  iPad mini 2, a consumer of the clocks of its amplifiers, to which it
+  supplies MCLK.
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: dai-common.yaml#
@@ -56,6 +58,7 @@ properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
       - apple,s5l8960x-mca
+      - apple,s5l8960x-mca-tdm
       - apple,s8000-mca
       - apple,s8000-mca-tdm
       - apple,t7001-mca
-- 
2.50.1
